                        </orgName><p>‘Hunc librum Antonii dedit magister Thomas Herlow collegio de
                        Oryell in usum ibidem tenencium’ (f. 278, per The Dean’s Register,
                        390)‘Liber domus beate Marie de Oryell Oxon. ex dono Johannis Corff fratris
                        magistri Willelmi Corff quondam prepositi domus predicte’ (The Dean’s
                        Register, 390)Coxe comments: ‘ex dono, quoad partem priorem, Thomae Herlow,
                        quoad posteriorem Johannis, fratris Willelmi Corff, praepositi’ (Catalogus,
                        s.n.)‘It was used and annotated by William Griffith, fellow, who died Oct.
                        1512. [...] He noted the contents “W. Griffyth ao doi 1510” and also wrote
                        “Gryffith de bangor”. Some one else added to “W. Gryffyth socius collegii
                        dicti Oryell” the words “obiit mortem anno domini 1512o die octobris anno
                        regni”.’ (The Dean’s Register, 390)</p></provenance>
